rgin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":61.7,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.010370685667270327,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.2436750064846408,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":59.4,"_gate_incr_roic":0.05347855143126599,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":34.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.09050039405403026,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":63.5,"_gate_pool_share":-0.006343399728140464,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":37.5,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04598396039680819,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":48.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.09356470155230445,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":71.8,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.014487766524156283,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":27.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.012131990738265763,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":34.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00674886910841967,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":88.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.00116,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"NextEra Energy, Inc., through its subsidiaries, generates, stores, transmits, distributes, and sells electric power to retail and wholesale customers in North America. It operates through Florida Power & Light Company (FPL) and NEER segments. The company generates electricity from wind, solar, nuclear, natural gas, and other clean energy assets. It also invests in generation, storage, transmission, and distribution facilities; owns, develops, constructs, manages, and operates generation facilities, including renewables, nuclear and natural gas, and battery storage facilities in the wholesale energy market in the United States and Canada, as well as electric and gas transmission assets, and natural gas pipelines; provides full energy and capacity requirement services; markets and trades in energy-related commodities; and participates in the production of natural gas, natural gas liquids, and oil. As of December 31, 2025, the company had approximately 35,963 megawatts of net generating capacity; approximately 93,000 circuit miles of transmission and distribution lines; and 932 substations. It serves approximately 12 million people through approximately 6 million customer accounts on the east and lower west coasts of Florida. The company was formerly known as FPL Group, Inc. and changed its name to NextEra Energy, Inc. in 2010. NextEra Energy, Inc. was founded in 1925 and is headquartered in Juno Beach, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John W. Ketchum J.D. | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $7.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 17K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["NextEra Energy, Inc. is a large-cap utilities business with a $182.4B market cap on $27.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 71% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7095527415192514},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","43 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"NextEra Energy (NEE) Stock Could Be 14% Above Fair Value On Energy Hub Funding","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/nextera-energy-nee-stock-could-211940016.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999980.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.967,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NextEra Energy to participate in EEI Financial Conference","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/nextera-energy-to-participate-in-eei-financial-conference-302932423.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000780.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NextEra Energy Vs. AES Corporation: Utility Scale Energy Production Just Got a Major Blue Boost","source":"247wallst.com","link":"https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/11/06/nextera-energy-vs-aes-corporation-utility-scale-energy-production-just-got-a-major-blue-boost/","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793987145.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.654,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Constellation Energy Earnings Ahead: What Past Reactions Say About The Stock","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/constellation-energy-earnings-ahead-past-234505687.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794008705.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.818,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"3 Infrastructure ETFs Pay Dividends From Pipelines, Railroads and Toll Roads","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/3-infrastructure-etfs-pay-dividends-230331000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794006988.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.013,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Comstock Resources (CRK) Reports Third Quarter Results, Is It Still 13% Undervalued?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articl